  "conclusion": "The unchanged packed first-result consumer sends a real cancel frame. With a controlled delayed item-send acknowledgement while the native server is active, that frame aborts the operation after direct CLI-result settlement; unchanged process binding requests SIGTERM, unchanged WindowsJobOwner sends terminate IPC, and unchanged runner state calls the injected terminateJob. Draining terminal avoids cancel. If the server already removed the stream, the same late cancel is ignored and a fixture nonempty Job keeps the runner pending. No real Windows Job membership, browser closure, or incident causality is established."
